0..72 Comment "// A program decides two bounds on `cos (π/4)` and on `sin (π/4)`, and"
73..147 Comment "// encloses an angle of a gate. It works through `std.reals.Eff`, the host"
148..223 Comment "// interface of exact reals. Each value lies between `0.7071` and `0.7072`."
224..287 Comment "// The angle is `β₁` of the Euler decomposition of the gate."
288..290 Comment "//"
291..368 Comment "// No plan of field operations and cuts defines a transcendental real. So π,"
369..446 Comment "// the cosine, the sine and the angle of a point are builtin nodes of a plan."
447..531 Comment "// Four plans compare `10000 · cos (π · 1/4)` and `10000 · sin (π · 1/4)` with"
532..603 Comment "// `7071` and `7072`. The fifth plan\'s root is the angle `β₁` of the"
604..682 Comment "// decomposition for `α₁ = 1`, `α₂ = 1` and `α₃ = 1/2`. That angle is"
683..779 Comment "// `arg (cos h · cos x⁺, sin h · cos x⁻) + arg (cos h · sin x⁺, −sin h · sin x⁻)`,"
780..858 Comment "// with `x⁺ = (α₁ + α₃)/2`, `x⁻ = x⁺ − α₃` and `h = α₂/2`."
859..861 Comment "//"
862..940 Comment "// The host encloses each builtin by its rule at a precision that doubles, and"
941..1009 Comment "// the checker replays each step before the host replies. `gandr run"
1010..1086 Comment "// trigonometry.gandr` prints `holds` four times on one line. It then prints"
1087..1157 Comment "// the two ends of an enclosure of `β₁` no wider than `2^-16`, near"
1158..1235 Comment "// `0.4305285`. The same `decided` and `enclosed` run under a handler of this"
1236..1279 Comment "// source, a second model of the interface."
1280..1282 Comment "//"
1283..1362 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/elementary.rs` — the enclosure rules"
1363..1383 Comment "//   of the builtins"
1384..1457 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/comparison.gandr` — a comparison of a cut"
1459..1491 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
